{"seq":17,"slug":"c-language-programming","title":"C 语言编程","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming","rating":{"composite":4.2,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":4.5,"strategic":4.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# C 语言编程 简介\n\nC 语言是现代计算的基石。从 Unix 到 Linux 内核，从数据库引擎到嵌入式固件，从 Python、Ruby 等高级语言的解释器到几乎所有操作系统的系统调用接口，背后大多是 C 在支撑。它诞生半个世纪而历久弥新，原因在于它处在一个独特的位置：足够接近硬件，让你能直接操纵内存与字节布局；又足够抽象，让你不必每天与汇编打交道。理解 C，本质上是在理解计算机「真正如何工作」。\n\n本知识库面向已有编程基础的学习者，目标不是教你「又一门语法」，而是讲清 C 作为系统级语言的核心机制，以及如何用现代工程方法把它写得既高效又可靠。需要特别说明的是，本 hub 聚焦纯粹的 C，与讲面向对象和泛型抽象的 08_cpp-fundamentals 有意区分开来。C 的世界里没有类、没有 RAII、没有模板，你拥有的是少而精的原语，以及随之而来的全部自由与全部责任——这正是它值得被单独、认真对待的理由。\n\n为什么 C 依然重要？因为它是理解底层的不二门径。指针让你看清「变量其实就是一个地址」，手动内存管理让你直面分配、释放与生命周期，未定义行为则逼你认清编译器与硬件之间的真实契约。掌握了这些，你再去看任何高级语言的性能问题、内存模型或并发陷阱，都会豁然开朗。同时 C 仍是嵌入式、操作系统、高性能库和跨语言互操作（ABI、FFI）领域无可替代的工作语言。\n\n全书分四章，由内向外、循序渐进。第一章 C 语言基础打牢类型系统、运算符、控制流与函数的根基，建立对内存模型的初步直觉。第二章指针与数据结构是全书的核心难点，深入指针、数组、字符串与动态内存，并用它们手写链表、树、哈希表等经典结构——这是 C 区别于其他语言、也最考验功力的地方。第三章系统编程与标准库走向操作系统层面，讲文件 I/O、进程与信号、并发以及标准库的正确用法。第四章现代 C 与工程实践收束于真实开发：C11/C17 新特性、构建系统、测试、调试工具（如 Valgrind、sanitizer）与内存安全的工程纪律。\n\n建议按章节顺序学习：先夯实语法与类型，再攻克指针与内存这一核心关卡，然后进入系统编程把能力用起来，最后以现代工程实践把代码写得专业、安全、可维护。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"c-fundamentals","title":"C 语言基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/c-fundamentals","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"types-operators-control-flow","title":"类型、运算符与控制流：C 语言基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/c-fundamentals/types-operators-control-flow"},{"seq":2,"slug":"functions-and-scope","title":"函数与作用域","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/c-fundamentals/functions-and-scope"},{"seq":3,"slug":"memory-model-and-layout","title":"内存模型与布局 — C 程序在内存里到底长什么样","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/c-fundamentals/memory-model-and-layout"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"pointers-and-data-structures","title":"指针与数据结构","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/pointers-and-data-structures","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"pointers-and-arrays","title":"指针与数组：同源而非同物","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/pointers-and-data-structures/pointers-and-arrays"},{"seq":2,"slug":"structs-unions-bitfields","title":"结构体、联合与位域：同一块内存的三种解释","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/pointers-and-data-structures/structs-unions-bitfields"},{"seq":3,"slug":"dynamic-memory-management","title":"动态内存管理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/pointers-and-data-structures/dynamic-memory-management"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"systems-programming-and-stdlib","title":"系统编程与标准库","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/systems-programming-and-stdlib","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"file-io-and-streams","title":"文件 IO 与流","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/systems-programming-and-stdlib/file-io-and-streams"},{"seq":2,"slug":"process-and-system-calls","title":"进程与系统调用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/systems-programming-and-stdlib/process-and-system-calls"},{"seq":3,"slug":"c-standard-library","title":"C 标准库","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/systems-programming-and-stdlib/c-standard-library"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"modern-c-and-engineering","title":"现代 C 与工程实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/modern-c-and-engineering","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"c23-and-modern-c","title":"C23 与现代 C 特性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/modern-c-and-engineering/c23-and-modern-c"},{"seq":2,"slug":"undefined-behavior-and-safety","title":"未定义行为与内存安全","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/modern-c-and-engineering/undefined-behavior-and-safety"},{"seq":3,"slug":"build-toolchain-and-debugging","title":"构建工具链与调试","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/c-language-programming/modern-c-and-engineering/build-toolchain-and-debugging"}]}]}